<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00565.html">
<title>DSA-6643-1 pam-mysql - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00565.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-11-19</dc:date>
<description>Andrey Vasilevsky discovered that pam-mysql, a PAM module interfacing
with MySQL databases, did not properly handle PAM_DISALLOW_NULL_AUTHTOK.
Users with a NULL password were authenticated by the pam_mysql module,
contrary to the PAM specification.
&lt;p&gt;
This update introduces the &quot;nullok&quot; option. If enabled in the
configuration or on the module command line, it allows users with a NULL
password to get authenticated unless the caller forbids this via the
PAM_DISALLOW_NULL_AUTHTOK flag.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6643-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6643-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00564.html">
<title>DSA-6642-1 nginx - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00564.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-11-19</dc:date>
<description>Multiple vulnerabilities were discovered in Nginx, a high-performance
web and reverse proxy server, which could result in remote code
execution, denial of service, information disclosure or bypassing
verification of client certificates.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6642-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6642-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00563.html">
<title>DSA-6641-1 php8.4 - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00563.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-11-19</dc:date>
<description>Multiple security issues were found in PHP, a widely-used open source
general purpose scripting language which could result in the execution
of arbitrary code, denial of service, information disclosure, privilege
escalation or cross-site scripting.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6641-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6641-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00562.html">
<title>DSA-6640-1 openjdk-25 - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00562.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-11-19</dc:date>
<description>Several vulnerabilities have been discovered in the OpenJDK Java
runtime, which may result in the execution of arbitrary code,
denial of service or information disclosure.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6640-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6640-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00561.html">
<title>DSA-6639-1 openjdk-21 - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00561.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-11-19</dc:date>
<description>Several vulnerabilities have been discovered in the OpenJDK Java
runtime, which may result in the execution of arbitrary code,
denial of service or information disclosure.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6639-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6639-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00560.html">
<title>DSA-6637-2 needrestart - regression update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00560.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-11-19</dc:date>
<description>The update for needrestart announced as DSA 6637-1 introduced a
regression due to an incorrect backport when using notify-send to notify
a user session via dbus. Updated packages are now available to correct
this issue.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6637-2&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6637-2&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00559.html">
<title>DSA-6638-1 haproxy - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00559.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-11-18</dc:date>
<description>Several vulnerabilities were discovered in HAProxy, a fast and reliable
load balancing reverse proxy, which could result in HTTP request
smuggling, request routing errors or denial of service.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6638-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6638-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00558.html">
<title>DSA-6637-1 needrestart - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00558.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-11-18</dc:date>
<description>Armaan Sandh discovered that needrestart, a utility to check which
daemons need to be restarted after library upgrades, does not properly
validate process names and cgroup paths. A local user can take advantage
of this flaw for local privilege escalation to root.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6637-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6637-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00557.html">
<title>DSA-6636-1 libvisio - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00557.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-11-18</dc:date>
<description>It was discovered that missing input sanitising in libvisio, a library
to read drawings in the VSD/VSDX formats, could result in denial of
service or potentially the execution of arbitrary code.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6636-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6636-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00556.html">
<title>DSA-6635-1 libreoffice - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00556.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-11-18</dc:date>
<description>Multiple security vulnerabilities were discovered in LibreOffice, which
could result in denial of service, information disclosure or the
execution of arbitrary code if malformed document files or hsqldb
databases are opened.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6635-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6635-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00555.html">
<title>DSA-6634-1 roundcube - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00555.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-11-17</dc:date>
<description>Multiple vulnerabilities were discovered in roundcube, a skinnable AJAX
based webmail solution for IMAP servers, which could result in IMAP
command injection, cross-site scripting, SSRF bypass, email header
injection, information disclosure, denial of service or privilege
escalation.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6634-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6634-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00554.html">
<title>DSA-6618-2 openexr - regression update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00554.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-11-17</dc:date>
<description>The OpenEXR security update announced in DSA-6618-1 failed to build on i386
due to test-suite failures. The missing i386 packages could also prevent
upgrades on multiarch systems with both amd64 and i386 versions of the
library installed.
&lt;p&gt;
This follow-up enables SSE2 floating-point code generation for i386. It
also makes test-suite failures non-fatal during package builds on
big-endian architectures. No additional vulnerabilities are addressed by
this update.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6618-2&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6618-2&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00553.html">
<title>DSA-6633-1 lightdm - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00553.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-11-16</dc:date>
<description>Matko ZlatiÄ? discovered a privilege escalation vulnerability in the Debian
version of LightDM, an Xorg display and login manager.
&lt;p&gt;
Due to a Debian-specific patch, the directory used to share data between the
LightDM and the users logging in was writable by the lightdm user of the
unprivileged greeter process. A process running under the lightdm identity
could leverage write access to that directory to force the LightDM process
(running as root) to change ownership and permissions on other root-owned
directories and escalate privileges from the lightdm user to root.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6633-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6633-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00552.html">
<title>DSA-6632-1 radsecproxy - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00552.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-11-15</dc:date>
<description>Two vulnerabilities were discovered in radsecproxy, a RADIUS protocol
proxy supporting RadSec, which could result in denial of service.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6632-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6632-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00551.html">
<title>DSA-6631-1 freedombox - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00551.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-11-15</dc:date>
<description>It was discovered that FreedomBox, a privacy-oriented home server, was
susceptible to privilege escalation.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6631-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6631-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00550.html">
<title>DSA-6630-1 pdns-recursor - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00550.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-11-14</dc:date>
<description>Multiple vulnerabilities have been discovered in PDNS Recursor, a
resolving name server which could result in denial of service or DNSSEC
validation bypass
&lt;p&gt;
Debian trixie previously provided the 5.2 release series which is no
longer supported upstream and since backports are not feasible this
update moves to the 5.4 release series.
&lt;p&gt;
Please refer to &lt;a  rel=&quot;nofollow&quot; href=&quot;https://doc.powerdns.com/recursor/upgrade.html&quot;&gt;https://doc.powerdns.com/recursor/upgrade.html&lt;/a&gt; before
upgrading.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6630-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6630-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00549.html">
<title>DSA-6629-1 network-manager-iodine - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00549.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-11-15</dc:date>
<description>Andreas Gabriel Berbescu discovered that network-manager-iodine, the
iodine VPN plugin for NetworkManager, did not properly validate the
nameserver setting when establishing a connection, allowing a local
unprivileged user to execute arbitrary commands as root prior to
privilege dropping.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6629-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6629-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00548.html">
<title>DSA-6628-1 linux - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00548.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-11-13</dc:date>
<description>Several vulnerabilities have been discovered in the Linux kernel that
may lead to a privilege escalation, denial of service or information
leaks.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6628-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6628-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00547.html">
<title>DSA-6627-1 libspreadsheet-xlsx-perl - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00547.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-11-13</dc:date>
<description>Several vulnerabilities were discovered in libspreadsheet-xlsx-perl. a
Perl module for reading MS Excel 2007 files, which could result in
denial of service or potentially the execution of arbitrary code if
specially crafted documents are processed.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6627-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6627-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00546.html">
<title>DSA-6626-1 c-ares - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00546.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-11-13</dc:date>
<description>Several vulnerabilities have been discovered in c-ares, an asynchronous DNS
resolver library, which may result in denial of service, DNS spoofing, or
information disclosure, depending on how the library is used.
&lt;p&gt;
These flaws include memory corruption issues (use-after-free, double-free,
and buffer overflows), excessive resource consumption during DNS message
processing, acceptance of replies from unexpected DNS servers, improper
reuse of cached answers with differing EDNS options, and the handling of
uninitialized memory for certain IPv6 addresses.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6626-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6626-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00545.html">
<title>DSA-6625-1 postgresql-17 - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00545.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-11-13</dc:date>
<description>Multiple security issues were discovered in PostgreSQL, which may result
in execution of arbitrary code, incorrect authentication, information
disclosure, denial of service or privilege escalation.
&lt;p&gt;
To completely fix CVE-2026-6460 some extensions will require
re-compilation against this released version, which will be scheduled
through upcoming trixie point releases.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6625-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6625-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00544.html">
<title>DSA-6624-1 sympa - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00544.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-11-13</dc:date>
<description>It was discovered that Sympa, a mailing list manager, is prone to a path
traversal and an unauthorized access bypass, which could result in
access to deleted or raw archive files.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6624-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6624-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00543.html">
<title>DSA-6623-1 tomcat10 - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00543.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-11-13</dc:date>
<description>Multiple vulnerabilities were discovered in the Tomcat servlet and JSP
engine, which could result in information disclosure, HTTP request
smuggling or denial of service.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6623-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6623-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00542.html">
<title>DSA-6622-1 firefox-esr - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00542.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-11-12</dc:date>
<description>Multiple security issues have been found in the Mozilla Firefox web
browser, which could potentially result in the execution of arbitrary
code, sandbox escape, privilege escalation, bypass of the same-origin
policy, information disclosure or spoofing.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6622-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6622-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
