<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00541.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-11-12</dc:date>
<description>Multiple security issues were discovered in Thunderbird, which could
result in the execution of arbitrary code or information disclosure.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6621-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6621-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00540.html">
<title>DSA-6620-1 apache2 - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00540.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-11-12</dc:date>
<description>Several vulnerabilities have been discovered in the Apache HTTP server,
which could result in remote code execution, denial of service and
information disclosure.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6620-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6620-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00539.html">
<title>DSA-6619-1 spip - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00539.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-11-11</dc:date>
<description>Several vulnerabilities were discovered in SPIP, a website engine for
publishing, which could result in unauthenticated remote code execution.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6619-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6619-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00538.html">
<title>DSA-6618-1 openexr - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00538.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-11-11</dc:date>
<description>Multiple vulnerabilities were discovered in OpenEXR, a library for handling
high dynamic range images. Processing malformed image files could cause
denial of service or out-of-bounds memory reads and writes.
&lt;p&gt;
This update moves to OpenEXR 3.2 series while retaining compatibility with
the existing Debian trixie library ABI.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6618-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6618-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00537.html">
<title>DSA-6617-1 symfony - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00537.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-11-09</dc:date>
<description>Multiple vulnerabilities have been found in the Symfony PHP framework 
which could lead to a bypass of access restrictions, information
disclosure, XML external entity injection or denial of service.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6617-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6617-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
<item rdf:about="https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00536.html">
<title>DSA-6616-1 linux - security update</title>
<link>https://lists.debian.org/debian-security-announce/2026/msg00536.html</link>
<dc:date>2026-11-08</dc:date>
<description>Several vulnerabilities have been discovered in the Linux kernel that
may lead to a privilege escalation, denial of service or information
leaks.

&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6616-1&quot;&gt;https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/DSA-6616-1&lt;/a&gt;</description>
</item>
</rdf:RDF>
